    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several favorable matchups today, with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the card at a stellar 83.29 efficiency rating. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite 4.78 xERA matchup against Ober and a critical \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor that boosts his stolen base upside, providing the highest ceiling on our roster. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) provide high-floor production against vulnerable left-handed starters. **Luis Robert Jr.** in particular is seeing a significant 14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage, making him a primary target for counting stats as we chase production in a tight 5x5 race.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Jackson Merrill**, who fell just short of our 40-point efficiency floor with a 38.94 score. Despite his talent, the combination of a tough 2.92 xERA opponent and a disadvantageous left-on-left platoon split pushed him to the bench in favor of higher-projected starters like **Miguel Vargas**, who carries a 63.34 rating into his matchup against the soft-tossing Lodolo. Meanwhile, we are monitoring the 31% rain risk in the Woo start; if the weather clears, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (61.73) remains a high-leverage start, but managers should keep **Nasim Nunez** ready on the bench as an emergency pivot should the contest be delayed or postponed.",
